 {
  "file": "docs/help/ai-assistant-limits.md",
  "text": "---\nid: ai-assistant-limits\ntitle: Switching on the AI assistants and setting their limits\nroute: /crm/settings\nhelp_ids: [sending.switches, settings.agent-limits]\ntags: [ai, assistant, campaign builder, hub guide, limit, monthly limit, spending, cost, who can use, switch on, help bot]\nsummary: A platform superadmin switches the Campaign Builder and the Hub Guide on, sets how much each may spend per month, and chooses who may use the Hub Guide.\nrelated: [hub-guide, campaign-builder, sending-settings]\n---\n\n## Steps\n1. Open CRM Settings and find the Campaign sending section.\n2. Under Switches, tick Campaign Builder or Hub Guide to switch either on for this organization. Both start switched off.\n3. In AI assistants, read this month's spend for each, then set each monthly limit in US dollars.\n4. Set how many messages one conversation may hold and how many steps one Campaign Builder run may take.\n5. Under Who may use the Hub Guide, tick the roles that should see it. The Campaign Builder is always for platform superadmins only.\n6. Press Save limits.\n\n## Common mistakes\n- Only a platform superadmin sees the AI assistants section and can change the switches.\n- When a monthly limit is reached, that assistant stops for the rest of the month and says so. Raise the limit here to continue.\n- A limit of 0 stops that assistant entirely, which is different from switching it off: the switch hides it, the limit refuses its requests.\n"
 },
 {
  "file": "docs/help/campaign-builder.md",
  "text": "---\nid: campaign-builder\ntitle: Drafting a campaign with the Campaign Builder\nroute: /campaigns\nhelp_ids: [builder.open, builder.describe, builder.review, builder.build]\ntags: [campaign builder, ai, draft, describe, review, build, tasks, needs review, superadmin]\nsummary: The Campaign Builder drafts a funnel campaign from a plain description: its messages, what starts it, and any form or page it needs, plus a list of what a person must still do. Everything it creates is a draft that sends nothing.\nrelated: [campaigns-hub, funnel-wizard, hub-guide, sequences-steps]\n---\n\n## Steps\n1. On the Campaigns hub, press Campaign Builder. Only a platform superadmin sees it.\n2. Describe what you want to accomplish, such as giving away a guide and then inviting people to book a call. You can paste an example email for reference.\n3. Press Draft it, then read what it will create on the review screen.\n4. Press Build to save it as a draft campaign, or describe changes and draft again.\n5. Open the new campaign. Each item it wrote shows AI draft, needs review until you edit or approve it.\n6. Work through the follow-up tasks it listed, which also appear in Client Tasks.\n7. Activate the campaign yourself when it is ready. Its starting sources switch on with it.\n\n## Common mistakes\n- The Builder never sends, goes live, enrolls anyone or changes consent. It only drafts.\n- Messages the claims check flagged are saved anyway and marked needs review, with a task saying why.\n- Asking it to change a live campaign creates a new draft copy; the live one is untouched.\n"
 },
 {
  "file": "docs/help/campaigns-hub.md",
  "text": "---\nid: campaigns-hub\ntitle: The Campaigns hub and funnel campaigns\nroute: /campaigns\nhelp_ids: [campaigns.tab-funnels, funnels.new, funnels.list, funnel.status, funnel.save]\ntags: [campaigns, funnel, funnels tab, new campaign, status, draft, active, paused, archived]\nsummary: The Funnels tab lists every funnel campaign in your organization. A funnel campaign brings people in from an event, places them on your pipeline, and sends them a series of messages until they reach a goal.\nrelated: [funnel-wizard, sequences-steps, dry-run-vs-live, campaign-builder]\n---\n\n## Steps\n1. Open Campaigns from the sidebar and choose the Funnels tab.\n2. The list on the left shows each campaign with its status, how many steps it has, how many people are in it now and how many reached the goal.\n3. Choose a campaign to open it on the right, where you can change its name, status, pipeline, what starts it, its steps and how it sends.\n4. Press New funnel campaign to set one up with the guided setup.\n5. Change the Status to Active when the campaign is ready to take in people, then press Save campaign.\n\n## Common mistakes\n- A Draft campaign does nothing at all. People only enter an Active campaign.\n- Paused holds everyone where they are; Archived puts the campaign away. Neither sends anything.\n- Changes apply to people who enter from now on. People already in the campaign keep the steps they started with until they reach the next step.\n- If the campaign engine is switched off for your organization, you can still build campaigns, but nothing runs until a superadmin switches it on in CRM Settings, Campaign Sending.\n"
 },
 {
  "file": "docs/help/consent-unsubscribe.md",
  "text": "---\nid: consent-unsubscribe\ntitle: How consent, unsubscribing and STOP work\nroute: /crm/contacts\nhelp_ids: [contact.tab-consent, contact.consent-record, forms.consents]\ntags: [consent, agreement, marketing, service, unsubscribe, stop, opt out, suppression, do not contact]\nsummary: Every campaign message checks the person's recorded agreement first. Marketing needs agreement to marketing on that channel; service messages need agreement to service messages. Unsubscribing and replying STOP record a withdrawal at once.\nrelated: [contact-drawer, forms, sending-settings, dry-run-vs-live]\n---\n\n## Steps\n1. People agree by ticking a consent box on a published form. The Hub records the exact wording they saw.\n2. You can record an agreement made another way in the contact's Consent tab, with the words they agreed to.\n3. Each marketing email carries a one-click unsubscribe link. Using it withdraws marketing email at once.\n4. Replying STOP to a text withdraws texts at once. Replying START brings back service texts only.\n5. Before every send, the Hub checks agreement, do not contact, bounces and complaints, the send window and the marketing limit, and records the reason for each decision.\n\n## Common mistakes\n- Agreeing to service messages does not cover marketing.\n- A form can only add agreement. It never reverses a person's own earlier withdrawal.\n- An address that bounced or complained stays blocked even if they later agree again.\n- A text agreement counts only for the number the person typed on the form.\n"
 },
 {
  "file": "docs/help/contact-drawer.md",
  "text": "---\nid: contact-drawer\ntitle: A contact's timeline, consent and campaigns\nroute: /crm/contacts\nhelp_ids: [contact.tab-timeline, contact.tab-consent, contact.tab-campaigns, contact.consent-record]\ntags: [contact, drawer, timeline, consent tab, campaigns tab, where they came from, send decisions]\nsummary: Opening a contact shows tabs for their history. Timeline lists what happened, Consent shows what they agreed to on each channel, and Campaigns shows the campaigns they are in and every send decision.\nrelated: [consent-unsubscribe, send-log, campaigns-hub]\n---\n\n## Steps\n1. Open CRM, then Contacts, and choose a contact to open their drawer.\n2. Choose Timeline to see what happened with them, in order.\n3. Choose Consent to see, for email and text, whether they may receive marketing and service messages, and the record each answer comes from.\n4. To record a decision made outside a form, such as on a call, use Record a decision made outside a form: choose the channel, the kind, and whether they agreed or withdrew, write what they agreed to, and press Save record.\n5. Choose Campaigns to see where they came from, which campaigns they are in, and the send decisions made for them.\n\n## Common mistakes\n- The Consent tab reads the consent record, not the older yes or no fields on the contact.\n- Write the words the person actually agreed to. An agreement with no wording cannot be saved.\n- A withdrawal takes effect straight away and stops the messages it covers.\n"
 },
 {
  "file": "docs/help/dry-run-vs-live.md",
  "text": "---\nid: dry-run-vs-live\ntitle: Dry runs, live sending and the test contact allowlist\nroute: /campaigns\nhelp_ids: [funnel.live, sending.switches, sending.allowlist]\ntags: [dry run, live, live sending, allowlist, test contacts, real messages, go live]\nsummary: Every campaign message is a dry run until live sending is switched on. A dry run records exactly what would have been sent and sends nothing. Test contacts on the allowlist can receive real messages before a campaign goes live.\nrelated: [test-funnel, sending-settings, send-log]\n---\n\n## Steps\n1. While the Live sending switch is off for your organization, every message is a dry run.\n2. When it is on, only test contacts on the allowlist receive real messages, and everyone else still gets a dry run.\n3. To send a campaign for real to everyone who agreed, a platform superadmin ticks Live sending for this campaign in its Sending section.\n4. The test contacts are listed at the bottom of CRM Settings, Campaign Sending.\n\n## Common mistakes\n- A dry run still runs every check, so its recorded reason tells you whether the real message would have gone out.\n- Live sending for one campaign does not switch on any other campaign.\n- Email and text messages each have their own switch as well; with one off, that channel is not sent even when live.\n"
 },
 {
  "file": "docs/help/forms.md",
  "text": "---\nid: forms\ntitle: Building a sign-up form\nroute: /forms\nhelp_ids: [forms.new, forms.status, forms.consents, forms.embed, forms.save]\ntags: [forms, forms and pages, sign up, fields, consent boxes, publish, form address, embed, intake, source key]\nsummary: Forms and Pages holds the sign-up forms that create a contact, record exactly what the person agreed to, and start the right campaign.\nrelated: [consent-unsubscribe, campaigns-hub, sending-settings]\n---\n\n## Steps\n1. Open Forms and Pages from the sidebar and press New form.\n2. Give it a Name and a Form address, using lower case letters, numbers and single dashes.\n3. Check the Fields. Each field can save to the contact's first name, last name, email or phone.\n4. Write each Consent box exactly as the visitor will see it, and choose its channel (email or text) and kind (marketing or service).\n5. Leave Starts campaigns routed from empty to use form:<form address>, or type a different source key.\n6. Set the Status to Published when it is ready, then press Save form.\n7. Copy the Embed on a website snippet into the page where the form will live.\n8. On the campaign it should start, add this form under Starts from.\n\n## Common mistakes\n- A published form needs a way to create a contact (an email or phone field) and wording for every consent box, or it cannot be published.\n- Forms accept submissions only while form intake is switched on for your organization.\n- Keep an empty hidden field named website on the page. Real people never fill it in, and submissions that do are dropped.\n- Changing a published form gives it a new version; earlier submissions keep the version they answered.\n"
 },
 {
  "file": "docs/help/funnel-wizard.md",
  "text": "---\nid: funnel-wizard\ntitle: Setting up a funnel campaign with the guided setup\nroute: /campaigns\nhelp_ids: [funnels.new, wizard.progress, wizard.save-draft, wizard.activate-test]\ntags: [guided setup, wizard, new funnel, purpose, who enters, pipeline, messages, review and test, template]\nsummary: The guided setup walks you through a new funnel campaign in five steps, then checks it is ready and can run a test drive.\nrelated: [campaigns-hub, sequences-steps, test-funnel, campaign-builder]\n---\n\n## Steps\n1. On the Funnels tab, press New funnel campaign.\n2. What it is for: choose the purpose closest to yours and give the campaign a name. A note for your team is optional.\n3. Who enters: choose what brings a person into the campaign, such as submitting a form, and press Add this. You can add more than one.\n4. Pipeline: choose the pipeline, the stage people enter at, and the stage where the goal is reached. A pipeline is optional.\n5. Messages: start from a template or add a blank step, then write each message and press Preview to see it as a person would.\n6. Review and test: work through the readiness list. Anything not ready links to where it is set.\n7. Press Save as draft to keep it without running, or Save, set Active and test drive to switch it on and send your own test contact through it.\n\n## Common mistakes\n- Next stays disabled until the campaign has a name.\n- A source shown as not connected yet will not start the campaign until it is connected.\n- Setting the campaign to Active lets real people who arrive from its sources enter it. While live sending is off, they only get dry runs.\n- On a draft campaign, Run the guided setup again reopens these steps with what you already chose.\n"
 },
 {
  "file": "docs/help/hub-guide.md",
  "text": "---\nid: hub-guide\ntitle: Using the Hub Guide\nroute: /campaigns\nhelp_ids: [guide.open, guide.ask, guide.stepper]\ntags: [guide, help, ask, how do i, walkthrough, show me, take me there, help bot]\nsummary: The Hub Guide answers how to use the Hub, citing the help articles it used, and walks you through a task one step at a time. It only explains; it never changes anything.\nrelated: [campaign-builder, campaigns-hub]\n---\n\n## Steps\n1. On the Campaigns hub, press Hub Guide.\n2. Type your question, such as how to test a campaign, and press Ask.\n3. Read the answer and the articles it cites.\n4. When it offers steps, press Take me there to open the right page, and Show me to highlight the control to use.\n5. Do each step yourself; the Guide never clicks or saves for you.\n\n## Common mistakes\n- The Guide only knows the help articles. When none fits, it says so plainly and marks its general pointer as not from the help set.\n- It sees only which page you are on, never what is on the page, so describe what you are trying to do.\n- To have something built for you, a superadmin can switch to the Campaign Builder.\n"
 },
 {
  "file": "docs/help/pipelines-stages.md",
  "text": "---\nid: pipelines-stages\ntitle: Pipelines and stages\nroute: /crm/pipelines\nhelp_ids: [pipelines.board, pipelines.edit-stages, pipelines.new]\ntags: [pipeline, stages, board, drag, move to stage, entry stage, goal stage, stage emails]\nsummary: A pipeline is a board of stages that shows where each contact is. Funnel campaigns place people in an entry stage and stop when they reach the goal stage.\nrelated: [campaigns-hub, funnel-wizard]\n---\n\n## Steps\n1. Open CRM, then Pipelines, and choose the pipeline at the top.\n2. Each column is a stage. Drag a contact's card to move them to another stage.\n3. Press Edit Stages to add, rename or reorder stages.\n4. Open the pipeline menu at the top and choose New Pipeline to start a new one, optionally from a template.\n5. In a funnel campaign, choose this pipeline, the stage people enter at and the stage where the goal is reached.\n\n## Common mistakes\n- Renaming a stage keeps it the same stage, so campaigns that use it keep working.\n- Removing a stage puts it away rather than deleting it; campaigns that pointed at it should be updated.\n- A stage can have its own stage emails. Dragging a card into that stage sends them, separately from any campaign.\n- When a campaign's goal stage is reached, the campaign stops sending that person its messages.\n"
 },
 {
  "file": "docs/help/send-log.md",
  "text": "---\nid: send-log\ntitle: Reading the send decisions\nroute: /crm/contacts\nhelp_ids: [contact.tab-campaigns, funnel.test-drive]\ntags: [send log, decisions, why, reason, allow, deny, defer, waiting, refused, dry run, what was sent]\nsummary: Every message a campaign considers gets a recorded decision: allowed, refused, or waiting, with the reason in plain words. You can read them on the contact's Campaigns tab and, for test drives, on the campaign page.\nrelated: [contact-drawer, test-funnel, consent-unsubscribe, dry-run-vs-live]\n---\n\n## Steps\n1. Open the contact and choose the Campaigns tab.\n2. Under Send decisions, each line shows when, the channel and kind, the decision, and the reason.\n3. Allow means the message was sent, or recorded as a dry run when the line says dry run.\n4. Refused means it was not sent; the reason says why, such as no agreement to marketing on that channel.\n5. Waiting means it is outside the person's send window and will try again when the window opens.\n6. For a test drive, the campaign page shows the same decision with what was sent or would have been sent.\n\n## Common mistakes\n- Refused for the marketing limit protects the person from too many messages; it is not a fault.\n- A message the Hub is unsure was delivered is not tried again, to avoid sending it twice.\n- Message wording is only shown for test contacts on the campaign page.\n"
 },
 {
  "file": "docs/help/sending-settings.md",
  "text": "---\nid: sending-settings\ntitle: Campaign Sending settings\nroute: /crm/settings\nhelp_ids: [sending.settings, sending.save, sending.switches, sending.allowlist]\ntags: [campaign sending, sender, from address, sending domain, reply to, quiet hours, send window, frequency cap, marketing limit, switches, time zone]\nsummary: CRM Settings, Campaign Sending holds the sender, the hours messages may go out, how many marketing messages a person may get, the switches for the campaign engine and its parts, and the test contacts.\nrelated: [dry-run-vs-live, consent-unsubscribe, test-funnel]\n---\n\n## Steps\n1. Open CRM, then CRM Settings, and choose Campaign Sending.\n2. Set From, the Sending domain verified in Resend, and where replies go.\n3. Set the Time zone for people with none on file, and when the Send window opens and closes.\n4. Set Marketing messages per person at most, and In any number of days.\n5. Press Save sending settings.\n6. A superadmin can turn each switch on or off under Switches, such as the campaign engine, live sending, email, text messages and public forms.\n\n## Common mistakes\n- Until a real sending domain is set, no campaign email can go out live.\n- The send window follows each person's own time zone. A message outside it waits until the window opens.\n- The marketing limit counts emails and texts together. Service messages do not count.\n- Only a platform superadmin can change the switches.\n"
 },
 {
  "file": "docs/help/sequences-steps.md",
  "text": "---\nid: sequences-steps\ntitle: Writing a campaign's steps\nroute: /campaigns\nhelp_ids: [funnel.steps, steps.add, steps.kind, steps.preview, steps.save]\ntags: [steps, sequence, messages, email, text message, sms, wait, delay, send after, kind, marketing, service, preview, merge tags]\nsummary: A campaign's steps are the messages people receive, in order. Each step waits for its delay after the previous one, then sends an email or a text, or simply waits.\nrelated: [campaigns-hub, university-assets, consent-unsubscribe, sending-settings]\n---\n\n## Steps\n1. Open the campaign on the Funnels tab and find the Steps section.\n2. Press Add a step for each message.\n3. Choose the Channel: Email, Text message, or Wait. A wait step sends nothing and only adds time.\n4. Set Send after (hours): how long to wait after the previous step, or after the person enters for the first step. Zero means right away.\n5. Choose the Kind of message. Marketing goes only to people who agreed to marketing on that channel. Service is for confirmations, reminders and things the person asked for.\n6. Write the subject for an email and the message itself. You can use {{first_name}}, {{last_name}} and {{org_name}}.\n7. Press Preview to see the message with a sample name. Nothing is sent.\n8. Press Save steps.\n\n## Common mistakes\n- A step left without a kind counts as marketing, the stricter rule.\n- Do not write your own unsubscribe line or opt out text. Marketing emails get an unsubscribe link and marketing texts get \"Reply STOP to opt out.\" added for you.\n- A text message that is too long once names and the opt out line are added is refused on save. Shorten it.\n- Editing a message removes its Not previewed check; preview it again before you rely on it.\n"
 },
 {
  "file": "docs/help/test-funnel.md",
  "text": "---\nid: test-funnel\ntitle: Testing a funnel campaign end to end\nroute: /campaigns\nhelp_ids: [funnel.test-drive, wizard.activate-test, funnel.status]\ntags: [test, test drive, end to end, check a campaign, test contact, try it]\nsummary: A test drive puts your own test contact into a campaign through the real engine. Within about five minutes the first step runs, and the result and its reason appear on the campaign page.\nrelated: [dry-run-vs-live, send-log, campaigns-hub]\n---\n\n## Steps\n1. Make sure your test contact is on the allowlist in CRM Settings, Campaign Sending.\n2. Open the campaign, set its Status to Active and press Save campaign.\n3. In the Sending section, press Test drive with my test contact.\n4. Wait for the engine's next run, about five minutes. The result appears below the button on its own.\n5. Read the decision and its reason, and what would have been sent.\n6. To test what starts the campaign, submit its form yourself, or move your test contact into the stage it listens for.\n7. When you are done, set the campaign back to Draft or Paused if it is not ready for real people.\n\n## Common mistakes\n- A test drive only runs on an Active campaign.\n- If the campaign engine is switched off, the test drive reports that and nothing runs.\n- Your test contact is entered once per event. Running a test drive again while they are still in the campaign starts nothing new.\n- While live sending is off, the test is a dry run: nothing is sent, but the decision is real.\n"
 },
 {
  "file": "docs/help/university-assets.md",
  "text": "---\nid: university-assets\ntitle: Delivering a free University resource\nroute: /university-access\nhelp_ids: [assets.add]\ntags: [university access, asset, resource, deliver, free guide, private link, deliver step]\nsummary: University Access lists the free University resources a campaign can hand out. A deliver step sends a private link that expires and opens the page on university.neuroprogeny.com.\nrelated: [sequences-steps, campaigns-hub]\n---\n\n## Steps\n1. Open University Access from the sidebar and press Add an asset.\n2. Give it a Title, the Page on university.neuroprogeny.com it should open, such as a free lesson's sign-up page, and a short description.\n3. Keep Available to campaigns ticked, then press Save asset.\n4. In a campaign's steps, set What it does to Deliver a free University asset and choose the asset.\n5. Write the message. The private link goes where you write {{asset_link}}, or at the end.\n\n## Common mistakes\n- The page must be on university.neuroprogeny.com; other addresses are refused.\n- Links are only sent while delivery is switched on for your organization.\n- Each link is private to one person and expires, so it cannot be shared around.\n- An asset that is switched off can no longer be chosen for new steps.\n"
 }
